A file pyHanko 0.37 signed, which the signature tests verify. generate.py
writes signed.pdf from ../../golden/archive.pdf and the keys in ../sign, and is
part of this repository under its MIT licence. Its signatures are not
deterministic, so each run writes different bytes.

- signed.pdf: archive.pdf rewritten by pyHanko as one revision with its page's
  /Annots in its own object, a text field "remark" that is its own widget, and
  a signature field "author" locking every field but "remark" and "witness".
  Then three updates: the author certifies it with /DocMDP permission 2, the
  remark field is filled with its appearance stream rewritten in place, and
  the witness signs a new invisible field locking "remark". Every pyHanko
  update rewrites the XMP metadata stream and the information dictionary in
  place, and the author's adds the catalog's /Version and /Extensions.

The document embeds a subset of Liberation Mono, under the SIL Open Font
License 1.1, whose text is in ../liberation/LICENSE.
